==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|de|Kanacke}} {{sense|people of Mediterranean looks}}

===Etymology===
From Polynesian ''[[kanaka]]'' "human being". Brought by [[seafarer]]s, initially as an honour title since the Kanaks were considered to be loyal people.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Kanaken|Kanaken}}
# {{context|derogatory|lang=de}} term for people of Mediterranean [[look]]s, usually applied to the [[Turkish]]
# [[Kanak]] or [[Canaque]], a member of the [[indigenous]] [[Melanesian]] [[inhabitants]] of [[New Caledonia]] in the [[southwest]] [[Pacific]].

====Declension====
{{de-decl-noun-m|n|n|n}}

